  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat percentage younger is Nani's sister than Nani? Nani is 9 years old. Nani's sister is 20% younger than Nani.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Nani’s sister is stated to be **20% younger** than Nani.\n\nFor example, Nani is 9 years old, so her sister’s age is:\n\n\\[\n9-(0.20\\times 9)=9-1.8=7.2\\text{ years}\n\\]\n\nThe percentage younger is therefore:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{20\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Nani is 8 years old.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Nani’s sister is still **20% younger** than Nani.\n\nHer age is:\n\n\\[\n8-(0.20\\times 8)=8-1.6=6.4\\text{ years}\n\\]\n\nSo, the answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{20\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Nani's sister is 25% younger than Nani.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Nani’s sister is **25% younger** than Nani.\n\nSince Nani is 8 years old:\n\n\\[\n25\\% \\times 8 = 2\n\\]\n\nSo her sister is:\n\n\\[\n8-2=6\\text{ years old}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the percentage younger is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{25\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: Nani's sister's age is compared with Nani's age using Nani's age as the reference.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Using Nani’s age as the reference:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\text{Nani's age}-\\text{sister's age}}{\\text{Nani's age}}\\times 100\n=\n\\frac{8-6}{8}\\times 100\n=\n25\\%\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Nani’s sister is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{25\\%\\text{ younger}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How old will Nani be when her sister turns 10? Also, here's some relevant info: Nani's sister is currently 6 years old.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Nani is currently 8, and her sister is 6, so the age difference is:\n\n\\[\n8-6=2\\text{ years}\n\\]\n\nWhen Nani’s sister turns 10, Nani will be:\n\n\\[\n10+2=12\\text{ years old}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{12\\text{ years old}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Nani and her sister will age by one year each year.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since both Nani and her sister age by one year each year, their **2-year age difference stays the same**.\n\n- Sister’s current age: \\(6\\)\n- Years until she turns 10: \\(10-6=4\\)\n- Nani’s age then: \\(8+4=12\\)\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{12\\text{ years old}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: What is the total age of Nani, Nani's brother, and Nani's sister? By the way, Nani's brother is twice Nani's age.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Nani is \\(8\\) years old, and her sister is \\(6\\).\n\nNani’s brother is twice Nani’s age:\n\n\\[\n2\\times 8=16\n\\]\n\nTherefore, their total age is:\n\n\\[\n8+6+16=30\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{30\\text{ years}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
